WOLF3D(1)

NAME
    wolf3d - launch the native Wolfenstein 3-D upstream port

SYNOPSIS
    wolf3d [upstream-options]

DESCRIPTION
    Starts the generated id-Software Wolfenstein 3-D source port through the
    SmallOS DOS/VGA/input compatibility shims.  This command is intentionally
    a thin entrypoint: it changes to /usr/share/wolf3d, passes argv through to
    the renamed upstream main function, and lets the original engine run on
    the SmallOS compatibility surface.

    Current builds reach the sign-on, title/menu, and early gameplay paths
    with staged Wolfenstein 3-D data.  The port stores CONFIG. in the original
    DOS-width layout and releases display/input ownership before returning to
    the shell.

    Bounded startup probes and status checks live in wolf3d-srcprobe under
    usr/libexec/tests.

FILES
    /usr/share/wolf3d
        Runtime data directory used by the port.

    third_party/wolf3d
        Upstream id-Software source submodule.  SmallOS-owned port code should
        stay outside this tree.

NOTES
    This is a work-in-progress native port of the original Borland C89/DOS
    source, not a rewritten clone.  Use a graphical QEMU backend and grab the
    guest window before testing mouse-driven gameplay.

SEE ALSO
    fractint(1), mandel(1), plasma(1), smallos(7)
